page (and ApiPlayground, DiskForecast, …) ship and which `Sources` already lists as a
project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Notifications/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Notifications`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same
reconciliation the sibling admin-AuditLog / DiskForecast / SchemaDrift logs recorded; it is
the only deviation from the literal prompt path.

TYPE-NAME RECONCILIATION: a pre-existing `public struct AuditLogPage` already ships at
`Sources/Features/Admin/AuditLogPage.swift` (the rich admin audit page, web route
`/admin/audit-log`). Swift top-level types are module-scoped, so the new notifications page
is named `NotificationsAuditLogPage` (model `NotificationsAuditLogPageModel`, etc.) to avoid
an invalid redeclaration. This is the distinct, simpler page the web moved to
`/notifications/audit` (its source comment: "Replaces the audit log panel that used to live
on the now-deleted /admin page"); both pages coexist in web (App.tsx L371 NotificationsAudit
+ L447 AuditLogAdmin) and now in Apple. The wire model mirrors the web `AuditLogEntry`
(`web/src/types/admin.ts`: id/action/resource/details/createdAt) — collision-swept against
Sources/Tests (0 clashes for all new public type names).

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/notifications/audit` is nested (App.tsx L371). A dedicated
`.notificationsAudit` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment `notifications/audit` → `.path`
`/notifications/audit` matching web exactly; Operations group alongside `.notifications`;
icon `clock.arrow.circlepath`), `AppRouteParser` aliases `/notifications/audit` →
`.notificationsAudit` (required — the generic first-segment fallback would otherwise resolve
`.notifications`), and `NotificationsAuditLogRouteRegistration` hosts the page, chained into
`\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift right after the admin AuditLog registration. So the page
is reachable via the Operations-group sidebar entry and any `/notifications/audit` deep link.
(Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

